# UX-SPEC.md §3.11 · §2.7 — a toast that points somewhere is clickable: `Created …` carries a
# `View` button showing `J` that opens the Jobs panel, as `J` does. Every toast has a ✕, and a
# toast the pointer rests on does not decay.
#
# `job success` is a real `CreateWorktree` through the run's own client (§2): with the Jobs panel
# closed its success is announced by a toast pointing at the panel. The dwell is the app's own
# clock, so `advance` moves it without a sleep (§1).
fixture: one-repo
await idle 30000
assert toasts[0] absent

job success
await toasts[0].text ~= "^Created " 30000
assert targets["toasts.toast[0].action"] exists && targets["toasts.toast[0].close"] exists

# Hovering holds the dwell: far past 3.2 s, the toast is still up while the pointer is on it.
hover toasts.toast[0] 200
advance 20000
assert toasts[0].text ~= "^Created "
shot toast

# `View` opens what the toast points at, and the toast has done its job.
click toasts.toast[0].action
await overlay == Jobs 5000
assert toasts[0] absent && key_contexts[0] == "Jobs"
key escape
await overlay absent 5000

# A toast that points nowhere has no `View`, only its ✕, which takes it down at once.
key y
await toasts[0].text == "Path copied" 15000
assert targets["toasts.toast[0].action"] absent && targets["toasts.toast[0].close"] exists
click toasts.toast[0].close
await toasts[0] absent 5000
dump dismissed
quit
